        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The repeated name"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Ravi went to the shop. Ravi bought milk. Ravi came home.\n\"Why say Ravi again and again?\" asked Amma. \"Say he.\""
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "pronoun",
          "he",
          "she",
          "they"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A pronoun takes the place of a noun. I, you, he, she, it, we and they are pronouns.\nWe use he for a boy, she for a girl and it for a thing or animal. We and they are for many.\nRavi went to the shop. He bought milk. The pronoun he stops us repeating Ravi."
        }
      },
